FP6: photos showed rotated in the photo roll slideshow. The camera saves the
sensor frame with an EXIF Orientation tag (grid thumbnails from
lomiri-thumbnailer are upright). Without Lomiri.Components.Extras the slideshow
loads the plain file URL; Lomiri.Components rewrites local image files to
image://scaling when the device pixel ratio is not 1 (Lomiri on Mir: wl_output
scale 3), and that provider ignores EXIF and autoTransform (checked with a QML
probe: DPR 1 -> 1536x2048, DPR 3 + Lomiri.Components -> 682x512 unrotated).
Load photos through the thumbnailer instead (EXIF aware), and set
autoTransform anyway.

--- a/qml/components/SlideshowView.qml	2026-10-26 13:26:14.710964636 +0200
+++ b/qml/components/SlideshowView.qml	2026-10-26 13:44:19.119928373 +0200
@@ -262,10 +262,15 @@
                         height: flickable.height * flickable.sizeScale
 
                         property bool isVideo: MimeTypeMapper.mimeTypeToContentType(fileType) === ContentType.Videos
-                        property string photoUrl: editingAvailable ? "image://photo/%1".arg(fileURL.toString()) : fileURL.toString()
+                        // FP6: not the plain file URL. Lomiri.Components intercepts local
+                        // image files at device pixel ratio != 1 (image://scaling), and that
+                        // path ignores EXIF Orientation; the thumbnailer applies it.
+                        property string photoUrl: editingAvailable ? "image://photo/%1".arg(fileURL.toString())
+                                                                   : "image://thumbnailer/%1".arg(fileURL.toString())
                         property string url: fileURL.toString().replace("file://", "");
                         Image {
                             id: image
+                            autoTransform: true   // FP6: honour EXIF Orientation
                             anchors.fill: parent
                             asynchronous: true
                             cache: false
@@ -282,6 +287,7 @@
 
                         Image {
                             id: highResolutionImage
+                            autoTransform: true   // FP6: honour EXIF Orientation
                             anchors.fill: parent
                             asynchronous: true
                             cache: false
